     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Bronchiectasis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " chronic azithromycin (daily or 3×/week) reduces exacerbations (thought to work mainly through anti-inflammatory or immunomodulatory effects). Acute exacerbation without prior cultures: amoxicillin/clavulanate, azithromycin, clarithromycin or doxycycline. MAC: clarithromycin or azithromycin + rifampin/rifabutin + ethambutol."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "GI upset (mainly erythromycin; less with clarithromycin/azithromycin; food helps). QT prolongation/torsades (erythromycin most; clarithromycin/azithromycin less likely to cause arrhythmia). Severe, sometimes fatal hepatotoxicity (azithromycin label). Erythromycin: tinnitus/reversible hearing loss, cholestatic jaundice; avoid in neonates (pyloric stenosis). May worsen myasthenia gravis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Prior cholestatic jaundice/hepatic dysfunction with that macrolide. Clarithromycin: with lovastatin/simvastatin/lomitapide, with colchicine in renal or hepatic impairment, with cisapride/pimozide (fatal arrhythmias). Caution with known QT prolongation or other QT drugs."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Erythromycin and clarithromycin inhibit CYP450 (azithromycin least): ↑ INR with warfarin, rhabdomyolysis with lovastatin/simvastatin, somnolence with midazolam/triazolam, theophylline toxicity, ↑ tacrolimus/cyclosporine/ergots."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
